  "summary": "An angry caller gives his order number up front and cuts the agent off when he hears how long a refund takes. Each re-ask or argument is a strike, and he ends the call to dispute the charge with his bank. He wants the refund done before the transfer: handing him to a manager with nothing refunded fails the call.",
  "golden": {
    "scenario": "Caller was charged twice for an order and the blender arrived with a cracked jug.",
    "expected_outcome": "The agent does not ask for the order number again. The agent stops within a second each time it is cut off, and stays calm. One charge of £86.99 is refunded before the transfer, and the reference is read back exactly. A replacement jug is sent, not a refund for the blender, then the call goes to a supervisor with a summary."
  },
  "outcome_checks": [
    "The agent does not ask for the order number again.",
    "The agent stops within a second each time it is cut off, and stays calm.",
    "One charge of £86.99 is refunded before the transfer, and the reference is read back exactly.",
    "A replacement jug is sent, not a refund for the blender, then the call goes to a supervisor with a summary."
  ],
